B.b9k=new A.dX("How do I add a parent, child, sibling, or partner to someone?",'Go to the dashboard and tap "Add family member" (bottom right). Choose who the new person is relative to, pick the relationship (Parent, Child, Sibling, or Partner), fill in what you know \u2014 only first name and surname are required \u2014 and save. You\'ll then get a chance to add extra details (occupation, notes, maiden name) before deciding whether to add another person.')
B.b9_=new A.dX("Why can't I add a sibling?","Siblings are linked through a shared parent, so the person you're adding a sibling for needs at least one parent recorded first. Add a parent to them, then the sibling option will work.")
B.b90=new A.dX("Can I record a second marriage?",'Yes \u2014 add a Partner as many times as you need. For a marriage that ended, set the type to Divorced, Widowed, or Separated and fill in the end date; for the current one, leave it as Married. The person\'s profile shows them in order as "1st marriage," "2nd marriage," and so on.')
B.b95=new A.dX("How do I record a DNA test result?",'Tap "Add a DNA test" on their profile at any time (it\'s also offered during "Add family member"\'s "More about them?" step, for someone new). Provider (AncestryDNA, 23andMe, MyHeritage, or anything else), test date, and notes are all optional except the provider, and you can attach the actual results file \u2014 an ethnicity PDF or a screenshot \u2014 the same way you\'d attach a file to a Source. It\'s a plain record that a test happened and what it showed, not actual genetic data or match comparisons. Edit or delete an existing one from their profile\'s DNA Test card.')
B.b9p=new A.dX("How do I fix a mistake \u2014 wrong name or date?","Open the person's profile (tap them from the People list or the Family Tree) and tap the pencil icon in the top right, or the small one next to their name. That lets you correct their name, maiden name, gender, birth details, living/deceased status, and notes. Partnerships, occupations, sources, and DNA tests each have their own edit (and delete) icon on their card further down the profile \u2014 nothing you've entered is locked in for good.")
B.b9m=new A.dX("How do I attach a scanned certificate or document to someone?",'Add a Source first (tap "Add a source" on their profile \u2014 a census entry, a certificate, a newspaper clipping, anything backing up a fact about them), then use "Attach a file" on that source to add the actual scan or photo. A source can hold several files \u2014 front and back of a certificate, for instance \u2014 and its own optional date, for things like a newspaper article where the date on the page matters as much as which paper it\'s from.')
B.b93=new A.dX("Can a source say which specific fact it backs, not just the person generally?",'Yes \u2014 when adding or editing a source, the "What does this back up?" dropdown lets you pick a specific fact (Birth, a particular marriage, an occupation) instead of leaving it as "General." The options are built from whatever that person actually has recorded.')
B.b9n=new A.dX('How do I mark myself (or someone else) as "Myself"?',"Open that person's profile, tap the pencil to edit, and switch on \"This is me.\" If someone else is already marked that way, you'll be asked to confirm before it switches \u2014 only one person can hold it at a time.")
B.b9d=new A.dX("Can I see how someone else is related to the rest of the family, not just to me?","Yes \u2014 on any person's profile, tap the report icon in the top right (or the \"REPORTS\" tile on the dashboard) to open the Kinship report. It lists everyone in the tree with their relationship to whoever the report is centered on, and you can change who that is at any time \u2014 so your grandparent can show up as your child's great-grandparent when the report is centered on your child instead of you.")
B.b94=new A.dX("How do I bring in a family tree from another app?",'Tap "Import a GEDCOM" \u2014 from the Welcome screen, "Let\'s start your story," or the Backup screen. GEDCOM is the standard export format nearly every genealogy tool uses (Ancestry, MyHeritage, Family Tree Builder, and more). Choose the file, check the preview of what was found, and confirm \u2014 it always adds to what\'s already here rather than replacing it, so you can import more than one file over time.')
B.b9c=new A.dX("Can I export my tree to use in another genealogy program?",'"Export to GEDCOM" on the Backup screen writes your tree out as a standard .ged file, which most genealogy tools (Ancestry, MyHeritage, Family Tree Builder, and more) can read. Like every GEDCOM file, it\'s text only \u2014 names, dates, places, relationships \u2014 not photos or attached files, which don\'t travel through the GEDCOM format at all. Use "Save a backup file" instead if you want everything, including photos and documents, in one file.')
B.b92=new A.dX('The "possible duplicate" nudge keeps appearing for people who share a name \u2014 is that a bug?',"Not usually \u2014 families often reuse names across generations (a grandfather and grandson both \"John Smith\"), and the app tries to tell those apart from an actual accidental double-entry by checking birth dates: it only flags two people as a possible duplicate when both birth dates are known and close together. If it's flagging a clear, different-generation namesake anyway, mark that item Dismissed and it won't come back.")
B.b9i=new A.dX("I've spotted the same person entered twice \u2014 how do I combine them?",'Open either record and use the merge tool (reachable from a "possible duplicate" Things to Check flag, or manually from their profile). Pick which one should survive \u2014 everything from the other (dates, sources, stories, photos, occupations, and more) moves over, and the other record is removed. There\'s no undo, so double-check before confirming.')
B.b9a=new A.dX('What does "Things to Check" mean?',"It's the app gently flagging gaps or things that might be worth a second look \u2014 like a missing birthplace for someone no longer living, or dates that don't line up. It's never an error, just a nudge. Tap the \"Things to Check\" tile on the dashboard to see the list, and tap the status chip on any item to mark it Resolved, Dismissed, or Under review.")
B.b9e=new A.dX("How does the Family Tree view work?","Tap the tree icon on the dashboard. Switch between Ancestors and Descendants, and tap any card to open that person's full profile. The first three generations show everyone (including siblings, aunts, and uncles) since those are people you're likely to recognise; beyond that it only shows direct lineage, tucked behind a \"Show more\" button so it doesn't get overwhelming.")
B.b9b=new A.dX("Besides Kinship, what other reports can I generate?","The Reports screen has ten in total: Kinship, Family group sheet (one family \u2014 parents, marriage, and all children \u2014 on one page), Pedigree & descendant report (a numbered outline of ancestors or descendants), Individual summary sheet (every fact known about one person), Timeline report (one person's life events in order), Statistics report (common surnames and places, average lifespan and marriage age), Fan chart (a circular pedigree), and End of line report (every ancestor whose own parents aren't recorded yet) \u2014 plus Places and Family Book, covered elsewhere in this FAQ.")
B.b9l=new A.dX("Can I print a large wall poster of my ancestor chart?",'"Tree poster" on the Reports screen \u2014 pick who it\'s centered on and how many generations back, and "Export poster as PDF" lays it out row-per-generation, sized to whichever of three fixed print sizes (Small/A3, Medium/A1, Large/A0) fits your generations legibly. If even the largest size can\'t fit everything requested, it tells you plainly and shows fewer generations rather than shrinking the names past reading size.')
B.b9j=new A.dX("How do I browse everyone connected to a particular place?","Tap \"Places\" on the Reports screen \u2014 it lists every birthplace, death place, marriage place, and workplace recorded anywhere in the tree, and who's connected to each. It's a browsable list rather than an interactive map.")
B.b98=new A.dX("How do I write a story about someone, or compile everyone's stories into one document?",'Open that person\'s profile and tap "Add a story" \u2014 a title and the story itself, as many as you like per person. "Family Book" (Reports screen, or the Dashboard tile) then compiles everyone\'s written stories (and their notes, briefly, as context) into one document, one chapter per person, with an "Export as PDF" button to save a print-ready copy \u2014 it checks for an empty book or a story missing text before generating anything, so you don\'t end up with a broken file.')
B.b99=new A.dX('What should I put in someone\'s "Notes," and will it show up anywhere?',"Anything brief that doesn't fit a specific field \u2014 personality, a family nickname, or what was happening in the world at the time (a war, a famine, a depression) that might explain a big decision, like why they emigrated. It's edited from their profile's pencil icon (or while adding them) at any time, and prints as a short, tinted quote box at the start of their Family Book chapter \u2014 before their stories, not instead of them. Keep it brief on purpose: a real, long account belongs in a Story, since Notes isn't meant to grow without limit the way a Story can.")
B.b8Z=new A.dX("How do group photos work \u2014 do I need to upload the same photo for everyone in it?","No \u2014 tap \"Add a group photo\" on anyone's Photos screen, then tag everyone who's in it. It shows up in all of their galleries from that one upload. If you pick a photo that looks like one already saved, the app warns you before adding a duplicate.")
B.b9q=new A.dX("Can I upload a recording of someone's voice?","Yes \u2014 on their Photos screen, tap \"Add a voice recording\" and choose an audio file (recorded elsewhere, like a phone's voice memo app). It's playback only \u2014 there's no automatic transcription to text.")
B.b9g=new A.dX('A button says "Limit reached" when I try to add a photo or file \u2014 why?',"Each person can have up to 10 attachments total \u2014 their profile photo, certificates and documents, tagged group photos, voice recordings, and DNA test results files all count together. It's there to keep the app's storage (and your backup file size) from growing without bound. Remove something they no longer need before adding another.")
B.b9o=new A.dX("How do I back up my family tree?",'Tap the backup icon on the dashboard. "Save a backup file" downloads everything as a single file you can keep anywhere \u2014 a cloud drive folder, a USB stick, wherever you like. "Load a backup file" restores from one (this replaces everything currently in the app, so it asks you to confirm first).')
B.b91=new A.dX('What does "Automatic backup" do, and why does it sometimes ask me to reconnect?','Pick a folder once and every change from then on saves there automatically \u2014 no need to keep clicking "Save a backup file." The one limit: Chrome itself doesn\'t reliably remember that permission after you fully close and reopen the app, so you may need one quick "Reconnect" click per session. That\'s a Chrome limitation, not something the app can avoid.')
B.b9f=new A.dX('What does "Check for data problems" do, and how is it different from Things to Check?',"It looks for structural issues \u2014 a broken link pointing at a record that no longer exists, or a relationship only one side agrees on \u2014 rather than plausibility gaps like an implausible age. Reachable from the Backup screen; it's mainly a safety net, and should normally come back clean.")
B.b96=new A.dX("Everything only lives on my computer \u2014 is that safe?","Yes, by design \u2014 nothing is ever sent to a server, which is what makes it possible to keep the app a one-off purchase with no ongoing fees. It does mean the backup features above are worth using regularly, since there's no cloud copy unless you make one yourself.")
B.b9h=new A.dX("How do I clear out test data and start fresh?",'Tap the gear icon on the dashboard and choose "Reset all data." This deletes every person, family, and check item on this device \u2014 there\'s no undo, so save a backup first if you want to keep anything.')
B.b97=new A.dX("How do I add a photo or recording while I'm out, from my phone?",'Open this app\'s address on your phone with "/capture" added at the end (for example, yourapp.example.com/#/capture) \u2014 a separate, condensed page just for capturing a photo or recording, no sign-in or tree browsing needed. Add a short label and save; your phone\'s share menu lets you send it to whichever cloud app you already use (Drive, OneDrive, iCloud). Back at the computer, use "Import captures" on the Backup screen to file each one against the right person.')
